# Test-only relaxations on top of the repository policy in //.clang-tidy.
# clang-tidy merges this with the parent file, so everything not named here is
# still enforced exactly as it is for product code.
#
# Each entry is a thing test code must be allowed to do and product code must
# not, which is why it lives here and not in the root configuration.
Checks: >
  -concurrency-mt-unsafe,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity

# concurrency-mt-unsafe
#   The CPU suite exists to exercise fork() and to report errno through
#   std::strerror. T3 forks on purpose with another thread holding a shim
#   lock; a test that could not call fork could not make that claim. The check
#   stays on for shim/, daemon/, cli/, fake_driver/ and common/.
#
# misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#   GoogleTest fixtures hand their state to TEST_F bodies through protected
#   members. That is the framework's interface, not our design choice.
#
# cert-err58-cpp
#   TEST/TEST_F expand to namespace-scope registration objects whose
#   constructors are allowed to throw. There is no version of a GoogleTest
#   file that satisfies this check.
#
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#   A TEST_F body is a straight-line list of assertions; its "complexity" is
#   the number of properties being asserted, which we want to be large.
